WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.279
- I didn't really know
what entrepreneurship was,

00:00:02.279 --> 00:00:03.863
but I believed that necessity

00:00:03.863 --> 00:00:05.064
is the mother of invention.

00:00:05.064 --> 00:00:06.363
I went out with those rocks.

00:00:06.363 --> 00:00:07.559
Some people didn't think that was cool;

00:00:07.559 --> 00:00:08.564
they had no need for me.

00:00:08.564 --> 00:00:10.195
People slammed the door
on me, cussed me out.

00:00:10.195 --> 00:00:12.421
We see so many people living day-to-day

00:00:12.421 --> 00:00:15.140
with so much money and popularity,

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.199
but they haven't built inner wealth.

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:20.226
You know, people believe
that opportunity knocks,

00:00:20.226 --> 00:00:22.109
you know, once or twice or annually.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:24.025
I would say opportunity never knocks,

00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:26.124
it's something you have to
go after with a vengeance.

00:00:26.124 --> 00:00:28.679
We're trying to be the next
this person, or that person.

00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:31.423
Be the next you, 'cause
everybody else is taken.

00:00:31.423 --> 00:00:33.138
It's important to always be prepared.

00:00:33.138 --> 00:00:36.053
I would say, if you stay ready,
you won't have to get ready.

00:00:36.053 --> 00:00:38.813
- He's an American businessman,
investor, columnist,

00:00:38.813 --> 00:00:40.356
author and motivational speaker.

00:00:40.356 --> 00:00:42.997
He began his entrepreneurial
career at age six,

00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:46.001
selling home-made lotion
and hand-painted rocks

00:00:46.001 --> 00:00:46.943
door-to-door.

00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:49.522
He was named on of the most
influential black men in America

00:00:49.522 --> 00:00:51.396
by the National Urban League.

00:00:51.396 --> 00:00:53.019
Here's Farrah Gray, and here is my take

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:55.140
on his top ten rules for success.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.876
Rule #5 is my personal favorite.

00:00:56.876 --> 00:00:58.449
I'm really curious to figure out which one

00:00:58.449 --> 00:01:00.366
you guys like the most.

00:01:02.971 --> 00:01:05.740
- How did you know, and how
did you have the wherewithal

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.956
at that age, that young,
to start selling things?

00:01:08.956 --> 00:01:10.377
I mean, you said you started selling rocks

00:01:10.377 --> 00:01:11.210
and people were like,

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.636
"Isn't that the rock that was by my door?"

00:01:12.636 --> 00:01:13.469
- [Farrah] Right.

00:01:13.469 --> 00:01:14.302
- And you sold it to them.

00:01:14.302 --> 00:01:15.658
You have the wherewithal
to do something like that

00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:17.005
and the courage.

00:01:17.005 --> 00:01:19.462
- Well I think that comfort
is the enemy of achievement.

00:01:19.462 --> 00:01:22.974
Growing up poor, when I
woke up, my mom was up.

00:01:22.974 --> 00:01:24.423
When I went to sleep, my mom was up.

00:01:24.423 --> 00:01:26.680
And my father was a
black leader and activist

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.739
and activism doesn't come with a salary.

00:01:28.739 --> 00:01:30.346
So I realized, I said, "Wait a minute,

00:01:30.346 --> 00:01:31.666
my mom had a heart attack, I said,

00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:33.331
I must do something to help her."

00:01:33.331 --> 00:01:36.284
So I went out and I sold oversized rocks

00:01:36.284 --> 00:01:37.153
that I saw on the streets.

00:01:37.153 --> 00:01:38.941
I would paint them and I would ask people,

00:01:38.941 --> 00:01:39.949
"Would you like to buy this?"

00:01:39.949 --> 00:01:41.193
And people would look at me
like, "Isn't that the rock

00:01:41.193 --> 00:01:42.651
that was in front of my door?"

00:01:42.651 --> 00:01:44.743
And I would say, "Yes, but it
can be used as paper weights,

00:01:44.743 --> 00:01:46.498
book ends and door stoppers."

00:01:46.498 --> 00:01:48.683
So I didn't really know
what entrepreneurship was,

00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:51.566
but I believed that necessity
is the mother of invention,

00:01:51.566 --> 00:01:53.167
so I got out there and I tried.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.052
And I think that, of
course as grandma says,

00:01:55.052 --> 00:01:56.998
"Nothing beats a failure but a try."

00:01:56.998 --> 00:02:00.868
I was well introduced,
very early, to rejection.

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:01.967
When I went out with those rocks,

00:02:01.967 --> 00:02:03.493
some people didn't think that was cool.

00:02:03.493 --> 00:02:04.488
They had no need for them.

00:02:04.488 --> 00:02:06.170
People slammed the door
on me, cussed me out,

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.025
all kinds of stuff.

00:02:07.025 --> 00:02:10.346
But I just made a few
dollars on that door,

00:02:10.346 --> 00:02:12.257
and then I said, "Well
let me go to this one,

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:13.090
I made some money there,

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.633
but the person in between cussed me out."

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:17.272
So you know, you kind of get
a chance to see very early

00:02:17.272 --> 00:02:19.569
that not everybody's going to tell you no.

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:22.553
A reallionaire is someone who
is rich from the inside out.

00:02:22.553 --> 00:02:26.291
We see so many people living
day-to-day with so much money

00:02:26.291 --> 00:02:30.008
and popularity, but they
haven't built inner wealth.

00:02:30.008 --> 00:02:31.957
So we see them getting
pulled over for DUIs,

00:02:31.957 --> 00:02:35.542
going to jail, living really,
I think, on what I call

00:02:35.542 --> 00:02:36.871
on a self-sabotage mission.

00:02:36.871 --> 00:02:39.348
But what I've discovered
is that you have to balance

00:02:39.348 --> 00:02:41.268
the inner richness and the outer richness,

00:02:41.268 --> 00:02:42.400
and that's what a reallionaire is.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.847
Someone who is rich from the inside out.

00:02:44.847 --> 00:02:46.442
Most people say that you
have to be at the right place

00:02:46.442 --> 00:02:47.564
at the right time.

00:02:47.564 --> 00:02:50.633
I always say, no, you have to
be everywhere all the time,

00:02:50.633 --> 00:02:52.482
because your visibility
is just as important

00:02:52.482 --> 00:02:53.716
as your ability.

00:02:53.716 --> 00:02:55.415
So, I think you have to show up.

00:02:55.415 --> 00:02:57.265
And I find a lot of
times, even personally,

00:02:57.265 --> 00:02:59.143
people are just not showing up anymore.

00:02:59.143 --> 00:03:02.331
You can't win if you don't
play, so we have to show up.

00:03:02.331 --> 00:03:04.531
- For example, right now
I find that people aren't

00:03:04.531 --> 00:03:06.774
showing up for their opportunities.

00:03:06.774 --> 00:03:10.149
You know, people believe that
opportunity knocks, you know,

00:03:10.149 --> 00:03:11.856
once or twice or annually.

00:03:11.856 --> 00:03:13.401
I would say opportunity never knocks,

00:03:13.401 --> 00:03:15.690
it's something you have to
go after with a vengeance.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.264
Living in Las Vegas, I even
give credit to people who

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:21.880
hit the jackpot there, because
at least they showed up

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.971
and put that dollar into
the machine for a chance.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.208
So I think you have to give
yourself a chance and show up

00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:29.629
in your relationships,
show up on your job.

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:31.361
Show up in life.

00:03:31.361 --> 00:03:33.424
I had a teacher tell me, I
told her I was going to be

00:03:33.424 --> 00:03:34.922
a millionaire entrepreneur one day.

00:03:34.922 --> 00:03:35.755
I was seven.

00:03:35.755 --> 00:03:37.421
She looked at me, she
said, "No you're not.

00:03:37.421 --> 00:03:38.436
You're poor and you're family's poor.

00:03:38.436 --> 00:03:40.071
You better go find somebody to work for."

00:03:40.071 --> 00:03:41.495
And she kind of pointed towards McDonalds.

00:03:41.495 --> 00:03:42.328
- Doesn't that make you go,

00:03:42.328 --> 00:03:43.366
"Hey, wait a minute, no, no, no."

00:03:43.366 --> 00:03:45.829
Doesn't that sort of
empower you even more,

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:48.874
or just give you the fuel
to prove that person wrong?

00:03:48.874 --> 00:03:50.469
- Well at seven years old, it didn't.

00:03:50.469 --> 00:03:51.559
I didn't know.

00:03:51.559 --> 00:03:53.393
I remember going home to
my grandmother and I said,

00:03:53.393 --> 00:03:54.669
"The teacher said I wouldn't be successful

00:03:54.669 --> 00:03:55.894
and I couldn't be successful."

00:03:55.894 --> 00:03:58.524
And she said, "Remember that
no matter what anyone says

00:03:58.524 --> 00:04:00.600
to you, wake up every morning
honey, and she's going to say,

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.604
'Why not me?'"

00:04:01.604 --> 00:04:03.814
"If you want millions, if you
want a mansion," she said,

00:04:03.814 --> 00:04:05.875
and prophetically, she said
if you want to put it into

00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:07.349
homelessness, and I've been the spokesman

00:04:07.349 --> 00:04:09.790
for the National Coalition
for the Homeless.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.934
When I found out the average
age of a homeless person

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:13.208
was nine and a half years old,

00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:14.880
I knew that I could give back.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.823
So she said, "Wake up
and say, 'Why not me?'"

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.676
She said, "If you believe in yourself,

00:04:18.676 --> 00:04:21.558
you can accomplish anything
that you put your mind to."

00:04:21.558 --> 00:04:23.596
I had a guy, he was 75 years old,

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:26.531
he called and he cussed me out.

00:04:26.531 --> 00:04:28.226
He said, "Farrah Gray!"

00:04:28.226 --> 00:04:29.326
I said, "Yes?"

00:04:29.326 --> 00:04:32.155
He said, "I've been working
on my ta-da-da life."

00:04:32.155 --> 00:04:33.588
Cut out the cuss words.

00:04:33.588 --> 00:04:35.247
President Hall, I didn't cuss.

00:04:35.247 --> 00:04:37.832
"I've been working on my ta-da-da life

00:04:37.832 --> 00:04:41.918
and why is it that you
have money for and I don't?

00:04:41.918 --> 00:04:43.575
I'm 75 years old."

00:04:43.575 --> 00:04:45.682
I said, "Because, sir,
you have to find what God

00:04:45.682 --> 00:04:47.775
put you here to do."

00:04:47.775 --> 00:04:50.278
The richest place in the
world is the cemetery, why?

00:04:50.278 --> 00:04:52.924
Because many of us have so many gifts.

00:04:52.924 --> 00:04:55.571
We're trying to be the next
this person or that person.

00:04:55.571 --> 00:04:59.237
Be the next you, 'cause
everybody else is taken.

00:04:59.237 --> 00:05:02.234
You have dreams, you have
seeds of greatness within you.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.702
You have the power to do
anything you want to do,

00:05:04.702 --> 00:05:07.823
but you got to put your mind in action.

00:05:07.823 --> 00:05:10.690
What I realized is that
there are two fights.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:12.171
There's the fight to make the money

00:05:12.171 --> 00:05:14.222
and then there's the fight to keep it.

00:05:14.222 --> 00:05:16.052
We've seen a lot of
people hit the lottery.

00:05:16.052 --> 00:05:18.078
William "Bud" Post, Evelyn Adams,

00:05:18.078 --> 00:05:20.894
which I talked about in my
book, "Get Real, Get Rich."

00:05:20.894 --> 00:05:24.544
They talked, we were
actually focused on the fact

00:05:24.544 --> 00:05:25.579
that they made all this money,

00:05:25.579 --> 00:05:27.151
they announced it to the world.

00:05:27.151 --> 00:05:29.075
They talked about it and
the next thing you know,

00:05:29.075 --> 00:05:30.964
they were broke.

00:05:30.964 --> 00:05:33.211
You have people that won the lottery twice

00:05:33.211 --> 00:05:35.428
and they live on public assistance.

00:05:35.428 --> 00:05:37.197
Those two persons, now
one's in a trailer park

00:05:37.197 --> 00:05:38.853
and the other's on public assistance.

00:05:38.853 --> 00:05:42.512
So, it's really about
studying what others have done

00:05:42.512 --> 00:05:43.659
as soon as they made money.

00:05:43.659 --> 00:05:45.783
Most people think that when
you get that television show,

00:05:45.783 --> 00:05:50.042
you're a big brand, that
money, that film opportunity,

00:05:50.042 --> 00:05:51.358
that that's the time to relax.

00:05:51.358 --> 00:05:52.990
I think it's actually time to work harder

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:55.288
and to multiply your success.

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:56.867
And you need to think,
I think, for generations

00:05:56.867 --> 00:05:58.106
yet unborn.

00:05:58.106 --> 00:06:01.842
So I had several mentors, one
gentleman introduced to me

00:06:01.842 --> 00:06:03.809
numismatics at an early age.

00:06:03.809 --> 00:06:05.601
He said, "Listen, young
man, if you really want

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:06.711
to make money,"

00:06:06.711 --> 00:06:09.103
he said, "have your children's
children's children's

00:06:09.103 --> 00:06:10.201
children thank you.

00:06:10.201 --> 00:06:11.224
This is what you need to do!

00:06:11.224 --> 00:06:12.171
Listen to me!"

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.896
I said, "Oh, okay, yes
sir, I listen to you."

00:06:14.896 --> 00:06:17.261
He said, "Follow my instructions.

00:06:17.261 --> 00:06:20.037
Invest your money in gold,
silver and platinum."

00:06:20.037 --> 00:06:21.605
I said, "Alright."

00:06:21.605 --> 00:06:24.007
I did that at a very early age.

00:06:24.007 --> 00:06:26.699
So it allowed me to really
learn the precious metals

00:06:26.699 --> 00:06:28.983
and the commodities market.

00:06:28.983 --> 00:06:31.361
You know, I studied Berkshire Hathaway,

00:06:31.361 --> 00:06:34.960
back when it was trading for a
few thousand dollars a share.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.667
So, I started making very
strategic investments

00:06:37.667 --> 00:06:40.465
because I realized, yes,
I may have this money now,

00:06:40.465 --> 00:06:43.005
but what will happen ten years from now?

00:06:43.005 --> 00:06:46.375
Ten years after that,
and now I'm 29 years old.

00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:50.105
I've had great sustainability
and I can still call myself.

00:06:50.105 --> 00:06:51.958
Some of my friends can't
call themselves that,

00:06:51.958 --> 00:06:54.125
but I can still call myself,

00:06:54.125 --> 00:06:56.340
by God's grace, a multi-millionaire.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:57.596
So I'm very thankful.

00:06:57.596 --> 00:06:59.852
- You were the youngest member
on the Board of Advisors

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:02.704
at the Las Vegas Chamber of Commerce.

00:07:02.704 --> 00:07:04.865
What kind of pressure was
that, I mean, to sit at this...

00:07:04.865 --> 00:07:07.029
It's a pretty big position, right?

00:07:07.029 --> 00:07:09.352
Did you feel prepared and
worthy of being there?

00:07:09.352 --> 00:07:10.259
Absolutely.

00:07:10.259 --> 00:07:11.092
- Yeah?

00:07:11.092 --> 00:07:12.983
- I think it's important
to always be prepared.

00:07:12.983 --> 00:07:16.296
I would say, if you stay ready,
you won't have to get ready.

00:07:16.296 --> 00:07:18.017
- So, being on the Board of the Las Vegas

00:07:18.017 --> 00:07:21.683
Chamber of Commerce, basically
gave me a front row seat

00:07:21.683 --> 00:07:24.852
of commerce and business and
also helping in assisting

00:07:24.852 --> 00:07:27.438
in making decisions, and of
course, some people looked at me

00:07:27.438 --> 00:07:29.989
like, "Isn't this kid, you
know, wasn't he born yesterday?"

00:07:29.989 --> 00:07:31.982
And I would say, yes, I was born yesteday,

00:07:31.982 --> 00:07:33.367
but I stayed up all night.

00:07:33.367 --> 00:07:35.723
A lot of times, warriors
and successful people

00:07:35.723 --> 00:07:39.118
have to continue sometimes
to walk alone, you know,

00:07:39.118 --> 00:07:41.232
and operate to the beat
of their own drums.

00:07:41.232 --> 00:07:42.776
- Yeah, that's true,

00:07:42.776 --> 00:07:44.426
and you keep good people
around you, right?

00:07:44.426 --> 00:07:45.303
- Absolutely.

00:07:45.303 --> 00:07:49.499
I would say, like the
legendary rapper, Chuck D,

00:07:49.499 --> 00:07:51.556
I say that if you can't
change the people around you,

00:07:51.556 --> 00:07:52.911
change the people around you.

00:07:52.911 --> 00:07:55.344
So I surround myself with good people.

00:07:55.344 --> 00:07:56.450
And some people are so negative,

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.417
I would say that they can walk
into a dark room and develop.

00:07:59.417 --> 00:08:01.445
- (laughing)

00:08:01.445 --> 00:08:03.094
- You got to make sure
you surround yourself

00:08:03.094 --> 00:08:04.607
with good people that build you up.

00:08:04.607 --> 00:08:07.414
Build that all-star team,
because when you feel like

00:08:07.414 --> 00:08:09.358
maybe I can't do this, or I can't do that.

00:08:09.358 --> 00:08:11.748
'cause one thing that a lot
of people don't understand

00:08:11.748 --> 00:08:12.774
about success, they ask me,

00:08:12.774 --> 00:08:14.785
"You know, is what you do difficult?"

00:08:14.785 --> 00:08:16.849
I tell them, what I do is easy.

00:08:16.849 --> 00:08:18.173
I mean, it is a piece of cake.

00:08:18.173 --> 00:08:21.996
The hardest part of what
I do now was the before.

00:08:21.996 --> 00:08:23.777
It was believing that I could do it.

00:08:23.777 --> 00:08:25.328
And that's the key.

00:08:25.328 --> 00:08:27.009
So when you have people
that encourage you,

00:08:27.009 --> 00:08:28.497
that build you up...

00:08:28.497 --> 00:08:31.041
Because a lot of times,
what they say sinks into

00:08:31.041 --> 00:08:33.200
your subconscious mind.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.711
A lot of people say,
"Okay, what do you mean by

00:08:34.711 --> 00:08:36.202
subconscious mind?"

00:08:36.202 --> 00:08:37.467
You hear a song on the radio.

00:08:37.467 --> 00:08:39.038
You know every single lyric to the song,

00:08:39.038 --> 00:08:41.035
but when it goes off, you forget it.

00:08:41.035 --> 00:08:42.132
So where were those lyrics?

00:08:42.132 --> 00:08:43.311
They were in your subconscious mind.

00:08:43.311 --> 00:08:44.641
Your dreams, some would say

00:08:44.641 --> 00:08:46.435
it comes from your subconscious mind.

00:08:46.435 --> 00:08:48.381
So when you hear people say
that you're not smart enough,

00:08:48.381 --> 00:08:50.174
you're not good enough...

00:08:50.174 --> 00:08:53.590
I had a teacher tell
me that I was too poor

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:56.624
and I wasn't smart enough
to be an entrepreneur.

00:08:56.624 --> 00:08:59.872
And recently she called and cussed me out.

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:00.705
She did.

00:09:00.705 --> 00:09:02.447
She said, "Why did you
put my name in your book?"

00:09:02.447 --> 00:09:03.563
- (laughing)

00:09:03.563 --> 00:09:06.097
- I said, "'cause I wanted
everybody to know who you were

00:09:06.097 --> 00:09:08.368
so you couldn't crush
anyone else's dreams."

00:09:08.368 --> 00:09:10.237
And like one of the greats
of our time once said,

00:09:10.237 --> 00:09:13.345
"Never allow anyone's perception of you

00:09:13.345 --> 00:09:14.803
to become your reality."

00:09:14.803 --> 00:09:16.182
What is it that we do best?

00:09:16.182 --> 00:09:17.913
I always say, find your
area of excellence,

00:09:17.913 --> 00:09:20.384
becaues the two most
important times I've learned

00:09:20.384 --> 00:09:22.831
is when we were born and when
we find out why we were born.

00:09:22.831 --> 00:09:24.304
What did God put you here to do?

00:09:24.304 --> 00:09:25.914
So ask yourself three questions.

00:09:25.914 --> 00:09:28.305
First question, what comes easy to me

00:09:28.305 --> 00:09:29.885
but harder to other people?

00:09:29.885 --> 00:09:32.921
Second question, what would
I do and do it for free?

00:09:32.921 --> 00:09:33.844
That one's tricky.

00:09:33.844 --> 00:09:35.601
And the third question is,
how can I be of service

00:09:35.601 --> 00:09:36.656
and how can I give back?

00:09:36.656 --> 00:09:38.285
And I believe that once
you're able to wrap

00:09:38.285 --> 00:09:40.987
those three things around
you and your philosophy,

00:09:40.987 --> 00:09:43.160
the world, the marketplace,
will open up for you

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.529
and share your gifts and your talents.

00:09:45.529 --> 00:09:46.749
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:46.749 --> 00:09:49.858
I made this video because
Marcelin B asked me to.

00:09:49.858 --> 00:09:51.750
So if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.999
to profile next, leave
it in the Comments below

00:09:53.999 --> 00:09:55.365
and I'll see what I can do.

00:09:55.365 --> 00:09:57.041
I'd also love to know
which of the top ten rules

00:09:57.041 --> 00:09:59.787
that we featured had the
biggest impact on you and why.

00:09:59.787 --> 00:10:01.594
What are you going to change
now in your business or life

00:10:01.594 --> 00:10:03.336
because you watched this video?

00:10:03.336 --> 00:10:06.445
Leave it in the Comments and
I will join in the discussion.

00:10:06.445 --> 00:10:08.033
Thank you so much for watching.

00:10:08.033 --> 00:10:11.533
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

